cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FusionCalib in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "FusionCalib: Multimodal Sensor Calibration for Robotics Rigs"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
authors:
  - family-names: Angadi
    given-names: Sarvesh
    email: sarvesh.angadi1997@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/sarveshangadi/fusioncalib"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >
  FusionCalib is a ROS2-native multimodal sensor calibration platform for
  robotics rigs. It solves extrinsic and intrinsic calibration across RGB
  cameras, depth sensors, thermal cameras, and LiDAR in a unified workflow,
  using a ChArUco board target and outputting calibration files compatible
  with ROS2 tf2, RTAB-Map, and ORB-SLAM3.
keywords:
  - calibration
  - robotics
  - ROS2
  - sensor fusion
  - extrinsic calibration
  - intrinsic calibration
  - depth camera
  - LiDAR
